note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note gpu/nvidia/checks/avv.om: the shared part of the avv-* checks, the view calls of CUDApp tests/attn_views_cases.c
note (the fixture of tests/attn_views_diff.c) and sweeps around them, compared with the pending C bodies of
note src/omega_attn_views.h (CUDAPP_MIGRATION_PENDING_ATTN_VIEWS). Each view unit carries om2 and is a program's head
note alone, so each has its own check: the unit, lib.om, lib-om2.om, its avv-UNIT.om (text t_name, text t_au, fn
note cname, fn avcap, fn avop) and then this part. Rows:
note   UNIT L n A B v X r h
note A and B are two arrays of L elements, each given as a b m k c p1 v1 p2 v2: element i is (a*i + b) mod m, or
note word i of X (16 hex digits each, - when unused) when m is 0 (A only); then c when k > 0 and i mod k is 0;
note then v1 at i = p1 and v2 at i = p2; cut to the element width (and, for f32, taken as its bits). avop runs the
note unit on the first n elements with the value v and must answer r; h is the FNV-1a digest
note (h = (h xor e) * 1099511628211 from 1469598103934665603) of the L elements of the array the unit writes, or of
note A for a unit that only reads. L above avcap (the largest local array of the element type, 4 MiB) is ckbad.
note element i of the explicit list X
fn avw i ulong to ulong
w = ulong 0
for j ulong 8
w = or shl w 8 ckhex 22 add mul i 8 j
end
ret w
end
fn avx s view ulong 9 i ulong to ulong
x = ulong 0
if eq get s 2 0
x = avw i
else
x = rem add mul get s 0 i get s 1 get s 2
end
k = get s 3
if gt k 0
if eq rem i k 0
x = get s 4
end
end
if eq i get s 5
x = get s 6
end
if eq i get s 7
x = get s 8
end
ret x
end
fn avgc d edit uchar * s view ulong 9 l ulong to void
for i ulong l bound 1000003
put d i uchar and avx s i 255
end
end
fn avgs d edit ushort * s view ulong 9 l ulong to void
for i ulong l bound 1000003
put d i ushort and avx s i 65535
end
end
fn avgu d edit uint * s view ulong 9 l ulong to void
for i ulong l bound 1000003
put d i uint and avx s i 4294967295
end
end
fn avgf d edit f32 * s view ulong 9 l ulong to void
for i ulong l bound 1000003
put d i bitcast f32 uint and avx s i 4294967295
end
end
fn avgl d edit ulong * s view ulong 9 l ulong to void
for i ulong l bound 1000003
put d i avx s i
end
end
fn avhc d view uchar * l ulong to ulong
h = ulong 1469598103934665603
for i ulong l bound 1000003
h = mul xor h ulong get d i 1099511628211
end
ret h
end
fn avhs d view ushort * l ulong to ulong
h = ulong 1469598103934665603
for i ulong l bound 1000003
h = mul xor h ulong get d i 1099511628211
end
ret h
end
fn avhu d view uint * l ulong to ulong
h = ulong 1469598103934665603
for i ulong l bound 1000003
h = mul xor h ulong get d i 1099511628211
end
ret h
end
fn avhf d view f32 * l ulong to ulong
h = ulong 1469598103934665603
for i ulong l bound 1000003
h = mul xor h ulong bitcast uint get d i 1099511628211
end
ret h
end
fn avhl d view ulong * l ulong to ulong
h = ulong 1469598103934665603
for i ulong l bound 1000003
h = mul xor h get d i 1099511628211
end
ret h
end
fn crow to bool
if or ne ckcnt 25 not ckis 0 t_au
ckbad
end
l = cknum 1
n = cknum 2
if or gt l avcap gt n l
ckbad
end
a = new ulong 9 0
b = new ulong 9 0
for j ulong 9
put a j cknum add 3 j
put b j cknum add 12 j
end
if eq get b 2 0
ckbad
end
if eq get a 2 0
if ne ckhexn 22 mul l 8
ckbad
end
end
o = new ulong 2 0
avop a b l n cknum 21 o
if ne get o 0 cknum 23
ret false
end
ret eq get o 1 cknum 24
end
